", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Matt Van Epps (R) is running."]}, "overview": "TN-07 sits in strongly Republican territory after redistricting, with a partisan lean of roughly eleven points toward the GOP. Matt Van Epps, who won the December 2025 special election in a closer-than-expected race, now runs as the incumbent against Nashville businessman Darden Copeland, who emerged from a contested Democratic primary. Independent candidates trail with minimal fundraising.\n\nNearly every professional rating service calls the district Safe or Solid Republican, with one at Likely Republican, and prediction markets give Van Epps about a 95 percent chance. Van Epps holds a large financial edge, having raised $2.3 million with substantial outside support, while Copeland has raised $870,000 but enters the fall with limited cash. No general-election polls are available, so the outlook rests on the district's lean and expert consensus. The expected margin is about eleven points Republican, with meaningful residual uncertainty given the district's recent competitive surprise.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0399, "margin": -11.34}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0635, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0506, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0512, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0318, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0486, "margin": -11.0}]}